# Vault — Hard Rules

Keep this file SHORT. Explanations and rationale live in ARCHITECTURE.md.

## Language & dependencies
- Go 1.21+; standard library only.
- Keep go.mod at `go 1.21` and never use language features newer than Go 1.21 (e.g. no range-over-int).
- No external dependencies without explicit user approval.

## MCP protocol
- MCP over stdio, JSON-RPC 2.0. stdout is reserved EXCLUSIVELY for JSON-RPC messages.
- ALL logging goes to stderr.
- Notifications (e.g. `initialized`) receive no response.

## Detection
- Local deterministic heuristics only; no external LLM or network calls.

## Testing
- Every heuristic gets table-driven unit tests with fixture inputs (testdata/).

## Definition of done
- Run `make verify` after every change; never claim a task complete unless it passes; show the output.

## Process
- Commit after each green milestone with a clear message.
- Work in small steps; propose a plan before large changes.
- Update .cline/memory-bank/progress.md at the end of every task.
- After a green commit, fast-forward main: git -C /home/vivek/Documents/ClineAiHackathon merge --ff-only <your current branch>, then run make -C /home/vivek/Documents/ClineAiHackathon build.
- At the end of every phase, execute docs/PHASE_CHECKLIST.md completely.

## Vault telemetry
- Telemetry is automatic: the Vault SDK plugin (`.cline/plugins/vault-telemetry`) appends every
  terminal command the agent runs to `.vault/activity.jsonl` via its afterTool hook.
  No manual report_activity calls are needed.
- To resume previous work, call vault read_handoff first.
